---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Authors" description="Who writes the notes. Open to the house.">
  <h1>Authors</h1>

  <p>
    Notes live in git. You write a markdown file, you put your handle in the
    frontmatter, you push (or open a PR). That is the CMS. No CMS.
  </p>

  <p>
    Path: <code>sites/tharavad/src/content/blog/</code>. Fields:
    <code>title</code>, <code>date</code>, <code>summary</code>,
    <code>author</code>. Plain text supremacy. If the site and the repo
    disagree, trust the repo.
  </p>

  <h2>Hands on the keyboard</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>alvin</strong>
      · maintainer
      · <a href="https://x.com/notrlyalvin">x.com/notrlyalvin</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>nihal</strong>
      · member
      · <a href="https://github.com/nihalsaeed">github.com/nihalsaeed</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Got a seat in the house? Add your name to this list when you land a note.
    We are not a sole-author brand kit. Members write. Git keeps score.
  </p>
</Base>
